          "category": "code_insight",
          "analysis": "This is a worm targeting MIPS-based Linux devices, likely IoT routers. It propagates by exploiting a known remote code execution vulnerability in Huawei Home Gateways (TR-064, likely CVE-2014-9222). The malware crafts a malicious SOAP request to the `/ctrlt/DeviceUpgrade_1` endpoint. The request contains a command injection payload in the `<NewStatusURL>` field, which uses `wget` to download and execute a secondary payload to `/tmp/.oxy`. It also contains functionality to discover other devices on the network via SSDP M-SEARCH requests.",
